  "hypothesis_id": "H64-L1",
  "lane": "Native-resolution LiDAR scarp channels + cultural-feature mask + 4-quadrant spatial CV",
  "hypothesis": "Aggregating native 1-3 m GeoDAWN/3DEP LiDAR Scarplet template matching (amplitude, relative age kt, orientation, SNR; Sare & Hilley JOSS 2018 + AGU 2015 T31A-2838 slope-aware templates) and Steger (1998) / Frangi (1998) multiscale Hessian ridge/valley line measures (2-20 m scales on a slope-detrended surface) to 100 m cells as scarp_pixel_fraction, snr_weighted_amplitude, structure_tensor_coherence, and dominant_strike\u2014then masking roads (TIGER), irrigation canals, section-line field edges, and mining benches (BLM) before retraining under 4-quadrant Leave-One-Quadrant-Out spatial CV with 20 km block calibration\u2014will produce a statistically significant (>2 SE) HOLDOUT-DTI gain on LiDAR-covered holdout blocks that is not confined to range fronts.",
  "mechanism": "Quaternary normal and strike-slip fault scarps cutting alluvial fans and intrabasin playas exhibit coherent 1-D diffusive curvature profiles across +/-21 m (3 m h_gate12) paired with sharp 2-20 m crest convexity and toe concavity (-LoG / +LoG Hessian eigenvalues) aligned along strike. Anthropogenic mimics (graded roads, canals, section-line plow berms) produce high 2 m short-wavelength slope excess but lack 10 m regional profile curvature and net 3 m far-field offset. Masking these cultural mimics and standardizing OOF spatial-CV probabilities within 20 km blocks reallocates dot budget from false-positive road/canal berms and saturated range fronts to genuine off-range-front intrabasin and piedmont fault scarps.",
  "named_non_fault_mimic": "Census TIGER road embankments/borrow ditches (tiger_road_distance_m <= 150 m), cross-slope irrigation canals (cross_max > 1.05*(upface_max + downface_max)), N-S/E-W agricultural section-line field edges (|sin(2*dominant_strike)| < 0.18 with h_gate12 < 0.10 m), and BLM closed mining claim benches (blm_closed_claim_distance_m <= 150 m) on low-relief/low-10m-curvature basin floors.",
